@startuml
' High-level runtime picture: what actually runs on a developer machine
' and how an external client reaches a service.
' Rendered into docs/architecture/overview.md.

skinparam backgroundColor transparent
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Segoe UI
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
skinparam ArrowFontSize 11
skinparam roundCorner 6

skinparam rectangle {
  BackgroundColor #FFFFFF
  BorderColor #7A7A7A
  BorderThickness 1
}
skinparam database {
  BackgroundColor #EEF4FB
  BorderColor #4A78A8
}
skinparam node {
  BackgroundColor #FAFAF7
  BorderColor #9A9A9A
}

title Runtime processes and how a client reaches a service

node "Developer machine" as dev {
  rectangle "Manager GUI\n(Electron / Web)" as GUI
  rectangle "FastAPI bridge\n(Python, one process)\n/api/grpc · /api/consul\n/api/nomad · /api/scaffold" as Bridge
  database "Consul agent\n:8500" as Consul
  database "Nomad agent\n:4646" as Nomad
  rectangle "Service A\n(gRPC :NNNNN)" as SvcA
  rectangle "Service B\n(gRPC :NNNNN)" as SvcB
}

rectangle "Other clients\n(CLI, Qt GUI,\nanother service)" as Client

GUI     <--> Bridge : HTTP / JSON
Bridge   --> Consul : Consul HTTP API
Bridge   --> Nomad  : Nomad HTTP API
Nomad    --> SvcA   : raw_exec
Nomad    --> SvcB   : raw_exec

SvcA    ..>  Consul : registers
SvcB    ..>  Consul : registers
Consul  ..>  SvcA   : health probes
Consul  ..>  SvcB   : health probes

Client   --> Consul : discover (Consul HTTP)
Client   ==> SvcA   : gRPC over HTTP/2
Client   ==> SvcB   : gRPC over HTTP/2

@enduml
